{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/residentclient owns the two sentences every surface says about an untrustworthy resident advertisement, so neither can drift from the other's account. Exact clean pushed head 4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9; tree ba161928, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's 7e55339e and my promise 85c73730.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH GAINS. Two exported constructors beside the ValidateURL that already lives here: UntrustedAdvertisement(reason) for the five classes the record itself fails — unreadable, larger than the 8 KiB a record may be, not a record at all, carrying no address, naming another workroom — and UnusableAdvertisedURL(advertised, reason) for the sixth, an address that is not a bare http loopback. That sixth is the one ValidateURL itself produces, so the sentence about it now sits next to the check that raises it.\n\nWHY THIS IS A SHARED HOME RATHER THAN A HELPER. Before this head the two sentences were written out in cmd/gs and nowhere else, and cmd/gitseq-mcp said nothing at all because it did not refuse. With the adapter now refusing too, the same six failures had to be explained twice. Two copies of a sentence about a security boundary drift, and the drift is invisible until someone compares the two surfaces on the same broken record.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. cmd/gs produces byte-identical output. I read the diff: the format strings are preserved verbatim and only the sentence moved inside the wrapper, so the existing invalid-advertisement tests in cmd/gs still pin the exact text. The way-out clause is deliberately not shared, because it differs by surface and must — gs offers --server -, and that flag is retired and ignored on the adapter, so repeating it there would be false.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"4990f83bb52a0052fdb1946fdd0edbced5c346e9","path":"internal/residentclient"}}